# TODO — features/project

- Invalid project addresses render silently (`routing/ReadableProjectRoute.tsx`
  `mainIssue`, `routing/ProjectRouteBoundary.tsx`): an unparseable URL such as
  `/p/<id>/works/revise-arc-3`, `/work/@slug` or `/chat/<id>` falls back to the
  chat index and keeps the bad URL, and the "This destination is unavailable"
  overlay does not appear on desktop even though `mainIssue` is `unavailable`.
  Show the unavailable state on the destination (and keep the URL). Found by
  the URL smoke probe (work item `thread-ux`, `url-smoke-screenshots/06*`).
- Open in Editor for Scratch and Uploads lands on the "not available yet"
  placeholder. Tracked in https://github.com/haowjy/meridian-flow/issues/625.
- Dock file slot is synced by effects (`dock/dock-view-store.ts` `workFile.active`,
  `enterWork`/`leaveWork`, the `ProjectView.tsx` layout effect, `DockShell`
  re-checks). Derive the shown file from the route's Work instead of syncing it.
  Deferred to a dedicated side-panel work item (mention-first peeking, #625),
  which also decides whether returning to a Work reopens its file.
